A||||9||mrfixit58||Need TPI 350 Opinion||||5||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||02-02-2001||12:36 PM||||I'm currently restoring a 68 RS Camaro. I have two motor/tranny choices: 350 carbed motor and TH350 tranny or; a 350 TPI and 700r4. I have both. The car will not be original since it came witha 6-banger and I'm going V-8. My questions are: Has anyone installed a TPI into a car that originally was carbed? If so, what kind of "challenges" could I expect? What would you do about the high pressure fuel pump? What about wiring? The TPI and tranny is coming out of a 89 Firebird GTA, what do I need to do to make my speedometer work? I can handle the transmission mechanical part of the installation because I've already done this to my buddy's 68 Camaro. But, this electronic stuff kinda baffles me.<P>Thanks for any help,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||buds||02-02-2001||01:22 PM||||I have a aftermarket wiring harness I bought from T.P.I tech for my V8 Fiero project that I have no time to finish. It is a plug and play unit. Only has the wiring a T.P.I. motor needs to run, also comes with a reprogramed corvette computer that tpi tech sais adds 25 HP, has a few other goodies too. Also have a K&N filter to fit your application. everything is brand new, let me know if your interested or want more info!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||02-02-2001||01:35 PM||||Roy,<P>Try this link... <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Speedway/4955/camaro1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Speedway/4955/camaro1.html</A> <P>This documents a 95 LT1/4L60 (same tranny) in a 68. He had a lot of the same issues as you.<P>Also try this one... <A HREF="http://members.tripod.com/~grannys/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.tripod.com/~grannys/index.html</A> <P>This is "Granny's Speed Shop/engineswap.com"<P>There are tons of swap links, including Fieros. <P>(Someone on here posted this a few weeks back, but it's worthy of a repost.) <P>Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||02-02-2001||02:04 PM||||Found another link... <A HREF="http://www.jagsthatrun.com/Pages/Stealth.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.jagsthatrun.com/Pages/Stealth.html</A> <P>Poke around a bit. They are selling modified 4L60 tailshaft housings. Think they may have what you need. <P>Also check here... <A HREF="http://www.jagsthatrun.com/Pages/Chevrolet_TPI_TBI_V-8.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.jagsthatrun.com/Pages/Chevrolet_TPI_TBI_V-8.html</A> <P>I bought their S-10/V-8 swap manual, a while back. Well worth the money.<P>Raydar<P><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 02-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||02-02-2001||02:16 PM||||Borders and Barns & Nobel sells several very good books on TPI engines. Check them out. I bought one on diagnostics because TPI electronics are very similar to Fiero's V6 (sensors, etc.). Also I'm sure there are Forums like these on Camaros. You can check in these Vette forums that I think may have some areas/links to it: <A HREF="http://corvetteforum.com/cgi-bin/Ultimate.cgi" TARGET=_blank>http://corvetteforum.com/cgi-bin/Ultimate.cgi</A>  <A HREF="http://www.c5-corvette.com/cgi-bin/Ultimate.cgi?action=intro" TARGET=_blank>http://www.c5-corvette.com/cgi-bin/Ultimate.cgi?action=intro</A> <BR>Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Will||02-02-2001||02:58 PM||||I think you should go with the TPI. Fuel injection is much better for efficiency, power, and driveability than carbueration. One item of concern: Are you trying to make this a Hi-Po engine? Stock TPI maxes out about 300-350 HP because of the diameter of the runner tubes.<P>My father is quite experienced with engine swaps. He and I are currently putting a TPI 400 into a 70's Jaguar. I'm sure he would be willing to give you some advice. Would you like contact info?<P>He's also developed a modification to an HEI distributor which would allow you to use the optical pickup from an LT1 distributor and run ANY HEI V8 with (DIY reprogrammable) LT1 electronics. The ditributor is still in the testing phase, though.<p>[This message has been edited by Will (edited 02-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfixit58||02-02-2001||09:16 PM||||Wow! Lots of great links. I'll have to do a little research to see if it's the way I want to go.<P>Will -- If I decide to go the TPI route. I'm sure I'll need to contact you. I espeially like the idea of the 400 TPI. I have a 400 block and was thinking about it as a TPI just today. Did you know that you can buy a stroker crank and bump the 400 to a 427? What a beast!<P>Buds -- Drop me a line and let me know how much you want for the TPI stuff.<P>Thanks guys,<BR>Roy   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by mrfixit58 (edited 02-02-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000007||rockcrawl||02-03-2001||08:56 AM||||Just a note about using an aftermarket harness. Make sure it incorporates an oxygen sensor. If the harness doesn't have provisions for an oxygen sensor the engine will run in open-loop mode with reduced performance. Also, if you have the complete donor wiring harness, it is not very difficult to adapt to another car. It looks like a lot of wires, but most of them just connect the sensors to the ECM. There are only a few wires that need to be connected to the cars electrical system.<P>I used the JTR S-10 book for a 350 S-10 swap. There was lots of good info but they seemed to be very biased on several things which I didn't like. I haven't seen thier TPI swapping book. I have a TPI book by Graffiti Publications which is excellent for the early MAF TPIs, but it does not cover the speed density systems at all. Your '89 GTA should be MAF.<P>The fuel pump and sending unit from the GTA should be easily modified to fit the early Camaro tank. another option is an inline pump from Holley for about $100 that they use with thier pro-jection systems.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Seanh||02-03-2001||03:32 PM||||Go TPI. I help a freind install a 350 in his 82 Z28. He blew the old 305 engine and put in a 350 crate motor. His old engine had Crossfire injection on it, we took it off and used it on the new engine. That thing has some power,  but it still looses to our Lincoln TownCar, but its got a 460 w/SEFI kit. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrfixit58||02-03-2001||03:33 PM||||Thanks Jon,<P>When I purchased the wrecked 89 GTA a couple of yers ago, I bought the JTR book on "TPI & TBI Engine Swapping". I was pretty disappointed. Mostly, it just says, "Buy a Helms manual for your car". Duh.<P>Regardless, I think I'm going to go for it. I have someone wanting to buy my carbed 350 so it looks like a "go". I may even wind up using the bul of the Firebird wiring harness. It still looks like a big job. I hope you guys will be willing to help me if I run into problems.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
